<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>R on Typophile Archive</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/r/</link><description>Recent content in R on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 28 Dec 2007 14:03:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/r/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Leg</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/40395/</link><pubDate>Fri, 28 Dec 2007 14:03:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/40395/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The stroke of &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131018043201/http:/typophile.com/wiki/capital"&gt;capital&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131018043201/http:/typophile.com/wiki/R"&gt;R&lt;/a&gt; projecting downwards from the &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131018043201/http:/typophile.com/wiki/bowl"&gt;bowl&lt;/a&gt;. Also found on capital K, lower case k. Legs vary in form, from straight lines to &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131018043201/http:/typophile.com/wiki/spine"&gt;spine&lt;/a&gt;-like structures with curled tips.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>